docs {
  # Create Work Experience
  
  Creates a new work experience block for your profile. This endpoint uses the batch update system, so you can create multiple blocks in a single request.
  
  ## Request Body
  
  The request uses the batch update format with a `creations` array. Each creation object contains:
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  |-------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `block_type` | string | ✅ | Must be `"work_experience"` |
  | `section_name` | string | ❌ | Section name (e.g., "experience", "work") |
  | `sort_order` | number | ❌ | Order within section (0 = first) |
  | `data` | object | ✅ | Work experience data (see below) |
  
  ### Work Experience Data Fields
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  |-------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `company_name` | string | ✅ | Company name (max 255 chars) |
  | `company_url` | string | ❌ | Company website URL |
  | `company_logo_url` | string | ❌ | Company logo image URL |
  | `position_title` | string | ✅ | Job title (max 255 chars) |
  | `employment_type` | string | ❌ | `"full-time"`, `"part-time"`, `"contract"`, `"internship"`, or `"freelance"` |
  | `location` | string | ❌ | Job location (max 255 chars) |
  | `location_type` | string | ❌ | `"on-site"`, `"remote"`, or `"hybrid"` |
  | `start_date` | string | ✅ | Start date in `YYYY-MM-DD` format |
  | `end_date` | string | ❌ | End date in `YYYY-MM-DD` format (required if `is_current` is false) |
  | `is_current` | boolean | ❌ | Whether this is your current position (default: `false`) |
  | `description` | string | ❌ | Job description |
  | `achievements` | array | ❌ | Array of achievement strings |
  | `technologies` | array | ❌ | Array of technology/tool names |
  
  ## Example: Current Position
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "work_experience",
        "section_name": "experience",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "company_name": "Tech Corp",
          "position_title": "Software Engineer",
          "employment_type": "full-time",
          "location": "Remote",
          "location_type": "remote",
          "start_date": "2024-01-15",
          "is_current": true,
          "description": "Building scalable applications",
          "achievements": ["Improved performance by 50%"],
          "technologies": ["TypeScript", "React"]
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Past Position
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "work_experience",
        "section_name": "experience",
        "sort_order": 1,
        "data": {
          "company_name": "Previous Company",
          "position_title": "Junior Developer",
          "employment_type": "full-time",
          "location": "New York, NY",
          "location_type": "on-site",
          "start_date": "2021-01-15",
          "end_date": "2023-12-31",
          "is_current": false,
          "description": "Developed web applications",
          "achievements": ["Shipped 3 major features"],
          "technologies": ["JavaScript", "Vue.js"]
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Example: Multiple Positions
  
  You can create multiple work experiences in a single request:
  
  ```json
  {
    "creations": [
      {
        "block_type": "work_experience",
        "section_name": "experience",
        "sort_order": 0,
        "data": {
          "company_name": "Current Company",
          "position_title": "Senior Engineer",
          "start_date": "2023-01-01",
          "is_current": true
        }
      },
      {
        "block_type": "work_experience",
        "section_name": "experience",
        "sort_order": 1,
        "data": {
          "company_name": "Previous Company",
          "position_title": "Engineer",
          "start_date": "2020-01-01",
          "end_date": "2022-12-31",
          "is_current": false
        }
      }
    ],
    "updates": [],
    "deletions": []
  }
  ```
  
  ## Response (200 OK)
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Version updated successfully",
    "data": {
      "version": {
        "id": 5,
        "version_number": 5,
        "created_at": "2024-01-16T15:00:00Z"
      },
      "created_blocks": [101],
      "updated_blocks": [],
      "deleted_blocks": []
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Notes
  
  - Dates must be in `YYYY-MM-DD` format
  - If `is_current` is `true`, `end_date` is not required
  - If `is_current` is `false`, `end_date` should be provided
  - Arrays (`achievements`, `technologies`) default to empty arrays if not provided
  - Each request creates a new version, preserving history
}

